---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="CentralD - Security-first homelab device manager"
  description="CentralD manages Windows and Linux devices from a single Ubuntu Server with outbound-only clients, a Tauri desktop Admin, and a typed, audited job pipeline."
>
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="hero-eyebrow">Security-first homelab management</p>
      <h1>One server. Every device. No inbound ports.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        CentralD is a device manager for private LAN and VPN deployments. An
        Ubuntu Server host manages outbound-only Windows and Linux clients
        through a Tauri desktop Admin application - with typed jobs, audited
        remote settings, and secure transient terminals.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/docs/quickstart">Get started</a>
        <a class="button" href="/docs/architecture">Read the architecture</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="quick">
      <div class="panel">
        <p class="panel-title">First-run path</p>
        <pre
          class="code"><code>sudo centrald-server initial-setup
sudo centrald-server config
# on each managed Linux device
sudo centrald-client enroll</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <p class="panel-title">What you get</p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Outbound-only client network daemon</li>
          <li>mTLS everywhere, no plaintext traffic</li>
          <li>Typed, leased, and audited job queue</li>
          <li>Verified, operator-approved updates</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="features">
      <a class="feature" href="/docs/architecture">
        <h2>Architecture</h2>
        <p>
          Three TLS listeners, one PostgreSQL source of truth, and a locked-down
          server-local control socket.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a class="feature" href="/docs/operations">
        <h2>Operations</h2>
        <p>
          Configuration, enrollment, renewal, jobs, shell sessions, backups, and
          recovery runbooks.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a class="feature" href="/docs/threat-model">
        <h2>Threat model</h2>
        <p>
          What CentralD defends against and what it does not, so you can deploy
          it with the right assumptions.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a class="feature" href="/docs/releases">
        <h2>Releases</h2>
        <p>
          Channel policy, immutable artifacts, Minisign verification, and the
          update pipeline.
        </p>
      </a>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    max-width: var(--content-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4.5rem 1.5rem 3rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .hero-eyebrow {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    max-width: 18em;
    margin: 0 auto 1.25rem;
  }
  .hero-lede {
    max-width: 42em;
    margin: 0 auto 2rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }
  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .quick {
    max-width: var(--content-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem 3rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .panel {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }
  .panel-title {
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .code {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .checklist {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  .features {
    max-width: var(--content-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem 3rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .feature {
    display: block;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }
  .feature:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .feature h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }
  .feature p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .quick {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
